prove-tests mutation for #59. Applied in CI only on a hand-run of the workflow with
`mutation: admit-anyone`, by `git apply` before Supabase starts: the edge runtime serves the
functions it compiled at start, so a patch applied later would never reach it.

It drops the admit function's roster check: an email that no people row carries still gets a
confirmed account, though nobody is linked to it. Everything else is unchanged.
Predicted: exactly one red, in admission.test.ts:
- "refuses an email on no roster, creating no account".
Every other admission case uses an email a people row carries, or is refused before the roster is
read. Any other result means the tests are not measuring what they name.

